      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "improve(control-ui): compress and cache bundled assets",
        "body": "Related: #105889\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nOperators loading the bundled Control UI transfer uncompressed HTML, JavaScript, and CSS, then revalidate fingerprinted bundles on repeat loads.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nVite now emits Brotli and gzip sidecars after every bundle rewrite, and `ui:build` verifies that every sidecar expands to the exact final asset. The Gateway safely negotiates those sidecars without request-time compression, while only package-proven bundled Vite assets receive immutable caching. Rewritten HTML uses a bounded four-entry compression cache; HTML, public files, and configured roots retain `no-cache`, and configured `.br`/`.gz` files remain directly accessible.\n\nAI-assisted: implemented and reviewed with Codex; I understand the resulting build artifact, Gateway negotiation, and cache boundaries.\n\n## User Impact\n\nThe bundled Control UI transfers substantially fewer bytes on cold loads, avoids request-time compression CPU for large static assets, and reuses fingerprinted assets without revalidation on repeat loads. Existing configured UI roots retain their current behavior.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Exact-head focused proof: 388 Gateway, 16 Vite-config, and 11 prepack tests passed (415 total).\n- Exact-head `corepack pnpm check:changed`: every selected guard, format, shrinkwrap, SDK, typecheck, lint, and changed-test lane passed.\n- Exact-head `corepack pnpm ui:build`: production build passed and verified 416 finalized Brotli/gzip sidecars byte-for-byte.\n- Testbox `tbx_01kxcvsvbbpwbxj2nkdnmwyte0`; Actions run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29224093009.\n- Earlier live Gateway measurement (`run_be6a4309705a`): identity/Brotli/gzip bytes round-tripped exactly; `index.html` 14,276 to 3,884 bytes with Brotli; entry bundle 782,854 to 205,088 bytes; bundled assets immutable and HTML no-cache.\n- Fresh final-delta autoreview: no findings; patch-correct confidence 0.89.\n",
